WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.830
The Lake District, in Cumbria.

2
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.700
Ice carved its valleys and lakes.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.990
38,993 people live in the National Park.

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:15.250
In 2025, 17.45 million visitors came too,

5
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.650
spending 1.784 billion pounds.

6
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.410
Herdwick sheep graze the fells.

7
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.590
Slate is still sold from Honister,
which now runs a zip wire too.

8
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.270
So who gets to use the fells?

9
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.290
The farmers, who were there first?

10
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.330
The tourists, who bring the money?

11
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.910
In this mission, you'll map the
four ways people earn a living here:

12
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.070
tourism, farming, forestry and quarrying.

13
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.830
Then you'll find where those uses
clash, and who wins when they do.

14
00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:48.930
Your mission: decide who should get
to use the Lake District's fells.
